  "id": "encoding-strategy",
  "term": "encoding strategy",
  "definition": "An encoding strategy is a way of helping information enter memory by organizing or linking it in a meaningful way. In the packet, this refers especially to a semantic approach that uses associations to connect new information with a person’s own context, which can support long-term recall.",
